{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Found the crash policy in the target's own contract rather than only in the launcher. The state machine interface documentation states that, apart from the abort-class errors, an implementation should return a non-nil error from SaveSnapshot or RecoverFromSnapshot only when the system needs to be immediately halted for a critical or non-recoverable error, with a disk error as the example. That is the requirement the save path implements when it panics, so the open dependency now has a documented obligation on one side: a recovering launcher would not just leave an undocumented residue, it would defeat the documented halting requirement. The snapshot-save account keeps its conditional classification because the mechanism that carries out the halt still runs through the pinned dependency, but its rationale, gap answer and counterevidence now separate the requirement from the mechanism, and the contract is recorded as a Fact.\"}"}}
